//
// A `lit` OF THE WRONG SHAPE IS REFUSED (`@FR-F-Target`, crossed with `@FR-F-Target-Kind`).
// `(F-Target)` calls `τ.lit(s)` for every literal run, so a target whose `lit` cannot take one
// text cannot be lowered — the author's bytes would have nowhere to go.  The refusal it owes
// has the shape `(F-Target-Kind)` gives a missing hole method.
//
// loft#2056: a `lit` of another arity still made the type a target, and every literal run was
// dropped silently — `"a{n}b"` logged only `I(3)`.
//
// @falsified-at: 88fb61b1f — hand-measured, interpret and native: the file compiles and `q.log` is
//   `["I(3)"]`.
// CHANNEL: expect — the diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the type, its `lit`'s arity and the shape it needs.
// HOLDS: a `lit(self: Q, s: text)` target is unaffected (each-hole-kind-calls-its-own-method).

struct Q { const log: vector<text> }

fn lit(self: Q, s: text, extra: integer) { self.log += ["L({s}{extra})"]; }
fn hole_int(self: Q, v: integer) { self.log += ["I({v})"]; }

// @EXPECT_ERROR: Q's `fn lit` takes 3 parameters
fn test_a_lit_of_three_parameters() {
  n = 3;
  q: Q = "a{n}b";
  assert(len(q.log) == 3, "unreachable: {len(q.log)}");
}
